“Gone Home” is definitely one of the best indie games of 2013. Once you enter in that home, you will find yourself in an extremely immersive place, which seems to be inhabited by real and believable people. Your surroundings seem to be alive and in every corner you will find something interesting to look at. And as you look into those details you will unfold an outstanding story that puts you right back into the 90s. Some people may complain about how short can it be, but those two hours I spent in that house were fulfilled with a kind of narrative that you rarely see in games.
You must play if:
-	you like games with an artistically approach;
-	you like a touching and human narrative;
-	you do not care about a short experience and simple gameplay mechanics.
